            <description><![CDATA[<h2>RestinPID 3.9</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>The list holds still while you use it.</b> When an app stops responding, Needs Attention no longer pushes the other apps down under your pointer, so a click can't land on the wrong app. New apps wait until your pointer leaves the panel; an orange count at the bottom shows how many.</li>
<li>An app that quits while your pointer is over the list keeps its row, dimmed and marked Closed, so the rows below don't jump up.</li>
<li>A click right after the list changes is ignored (you'll hear a beep), because it was aimed at the old layout.</li>
<li>The right-click menu names the app: "Force Quit Safari", not just "Force Quit".</li>
<li>The menu bar icon keeps the same width when it shows a count, so the icons next to it don't shift.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
